{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1765 (change 1765, commit 3d7ac906f7b).\n\nWhat landed:\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py: new ensure unit _untrack_runtime_markers_unit — check = one `git ls-files -- '*/.archived' '*/.write.lock'` (empty → ok, zero commits); act = batched `git rm --cached --quiet` (index only, worktree untouched, batch=200 to stay under ARG_MAX) + ONE commit. Enumerates ls-files output (not raw pathspecs) so a store tracking only one marker kind never fails on an unmatched pathspec.\n- src/rebar/_store/ensures.py: `untrack-runtime-markers` added to REGISTRY_IDS + _registry().\n- src/rebar/reducer/_api.py: reader self-heal _heal_missing_marker — on the exclude_archived list path, a net-archived ticket with a missing .archived marker gets it re-materialized via reducer.marker.write_marker (mirror of the stale-marker clearing); scoped so include-archived lists never touch markers.\n- tests/unit/test_ensures_untrack_markers.py (new, 10 tests): riskiest-first two-clone merge test proving the untrack commit merges cleanly into a diverged peer and git deletes the peer's worktree marker copies with clean status; happy path (ls-files empty, worktree intact, exactly 1 commit, 2nd run ok/0 commits, marker churn invisible to status); batching; single-marker-kind; fresh-store run_ensures ok/0 commits; registry wiring; re-materialize + excluded-from-default-list; no-marker-for-live-ticket; include-archived untouched; stale-marker-still-cleared.\n- Registry-count pins updated 8→9 (test_ensures.py, test_ensure_drift_matrix.py, test_fsck_ensures.py).\n- docs/migrations.md: one paragraph on the unit + reader self-heal.\n\nTDD: all new behavior tests written first and proven failing on unmodified code (7 failed / 2 regression-guard passes). Manual mutation pass: 10 mutants (invert check, drop commit, drop batching, drop pathspec, rm without --cached, wrong status, invert archived cond, drop exclude_archived guard, skip write_marker, write→remove swap) — 10/10 killed; one equivalent mutant noted (dropping the defensive check_marker guard is behaviorally identical since the loop guarantees marker absence at heal time).\n\nmake lint + make typecheck clean; complexity ratchet clean (new=0 increased=0); init.py at 795 LOC (cap 800). Known-environmental failures on this machine (global safe.bareRepository=explicit breaks bare-fixture tests: test_tracker_config_e2e, test_mcp_push_status, test_bridge_runner_install_paths_heldout) reproduced independent of this change.\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on change 1765; close after merge per policy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786685442289984001,"uuid":"99e9697f-b4e4-4aa7-83bb-e03711960a1e"}